# Jogania Application Environment Variables
#
# This file serves as a template for the required environment variables.
# To use these in a development environment, create a new file named `.env.local`
# and copy the contents of this file into it. Then, replace the placeholder values
# with your actual secrets.
#
# DO NOT commit the `.env.local` file to version control.
# The `.gitignore` file is already configured to ignore it.

# Example for a hypothetical external API integration
# VITE_SOME_API_KEY="your-api-key-here"
